# CONTROL topology: identical shape to rail_1024gpu_8rail.topo (32 leaves x 64 ports,
# 32 spines, 2-tier, non-blocking) but with CLASSIC CONSECUTIVE host->leaf attachment:
# leaf t owns hosts [32t, 32t+32) = 4 whole 8-GPU servers.
# Purpose: isolates the effect of the rail ASSIGNMENT from the effect of the
# leaf/spine SHAPE, by holding the shape constant. Diff this against
# rail_1024gpu_8rail.topo -- the only difference is the "Rails 8" line.
#   which is inverted vs reality. Negligible for scattered patterns (~0.7% of a2a
#   flows) but pessimistic for ring collectives. See notes/.
Nodes 1024
Tiers 2
Podsize 1024
# (no Rails line -> consecutive attachment: leaf = 4 whole servers)

Tier 0
Oversubscribed 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 32
Radix_Up 32
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 200
Radix_Down 32
Downlink_Latency_ns 1000
Switch_Latency_ns 0
Bundle 1
